# Definition of Done

A task is DONE when:
- Scope matches the assigned sprint document.
- No out-of-scope business behavior was added.
- Code follows project architecture.
- API/database/platform contracts align.
- Relevant tests pass.
- Negative paths are covered.
- Security/authorization requirements are verified.
- No secrets or sensitive logs are introduced.
- Documentation/contract changes are updated.
- Agent reports changed files, tests, risks and remaining issues.

A sprint is DONE when:
- All assigned platform use cases pass.
- Acceptance criteria pass.
- All required tests pass.
- No blocker/critical defect remains.
- Cross-platform integration is verified.
- QA signs off.
- Security review signs off where applicable.
- Orchestrator performs final acceptance against the sprint documents.
